{:edb/db-before-t 1487 :edb/db-after-t 1488 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534800 50 #inst "2026-10-08T07:20:41.239Z" 13194139534800 true] [17592186092114 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310808 13194139534800 true] [17592186092116 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310815 13194139534800 true] [17592186092116 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310827 13194139534800 true] [17592186092117 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310820 13194139534800 true] [17592186092569 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534800 true] [17592186092569 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040762/assets/f00d8bd6cbd1f113df7f023e161e4d79e2f4a81157d1ac9a8ab65e70b4959221.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.$  Find the $x$-coordinate of the point $B.$" 13194139534800 true] [17592186092569 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/915/Source/Images/q-20414.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y = \\tan x$ and the line $y =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$. Find the $x$-coordinate of the point $B$." 13194139534800 false] [17592186092569 1145 "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n$$\n\n Now, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis value lies inside $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi $ hence, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ This is the $x$ coordinate of $A.$\n\nTo get another solution, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Thus,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +x=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $B$ is $\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.$" 13194139534800 true] [17592186310808 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310809 13194139534800 true] [17592186310808 1089 "q-121127" 13194139534800 true] [17592186310808 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534800 true] [17592186310808 1100 "Solve the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=8$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ rounded to the nearest integer." 13194139534800 true] [17592186310808 1113 #uuid "9cd45f06-c66b-580b-8617-33b2a6b66d17" 13194139534800 true] [17592186310808 1145 "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(8)=82.874\\,983{…}^{∘}≈{82.87}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${82.87}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={82.87}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+{82.87}^{∘}={262.87}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are\n\n$$\nx={83}^{∘},{263}^{∘}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." 13194139534800 true] [17592186310809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310810 13194139534800 true] [17592186310809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310811 13194139534800 true] [17592186310809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310812 13194139534800 true] [17592186310809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310813 13194139534800 true] [17592186310809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310814 13194139534800 true] [17592186310809 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534800 true] [17592186310809 1041 "selection" 13194139534800 true] [17592186310809 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310813 13194139534800 true] [17592186310809 1110 #uuid "fabc99b9-5ea2-5ad4-8bd5-e2dd7f0f7d48" 13194139534800 true] [17592186310810 1034 "x={76}^{∘},{256}^{∘}" 13194139534800 true] [17592186310810 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534800 true] [17592186310810 1111 #uuid "cf942574-5afe-520f-af8a-2653cf6ba03e" 13194139534800 true] [17592186310811 1034 "x={70}^{∘},{250}^{∘}" 13194139534800 true] [17592186310811 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534800 true] [17592186310811 1111 #uuid "29a6a170-f56e-557a-9f9a-5c603988a9aa" 13194139534800 true] [17592186310812 1034 "x={63}^{∘},{243}^{∘}" 13194139534800 true] [17592186310812 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534800 true] [17592186310812 1111 #uuid "6e6568cd-5b34-5130-b80e-b2a441700382" 13194139534800 true] [17592186310813 1034 "x={83}